WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.000
When NBC decided to create a spinoff from
their hit series The Blacklist, they had the

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.019
perfect star in mind to headline the series:
Famke Janssen.

00:00:09.019 --> 00:00:13.579
After making her debut in the show's third
season, her character Susan Hargrave became

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.709
the focus of The Blacklist: Redemption.

00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:19.660
If you think you recognize her from somewhere,
it's probably because you've seen Janssen

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.610
in one of her dozens of film and television
roles.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:26.380
Here's why Susan from The Blacklist looks
so familiar.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.720
GoldenEye

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.739
Janssen got her start as a model in the late
'80s, but in the early '90s she decided to

00:00:32.739 --> 00:00:34.149
transition to acting.

00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:38.950
She soon landed small roles on shows like
Star Trek: The Next Generation and in films

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.760
such as Fathers &amp; Sons.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:46.120
But her big break came in the 1995 James Bond
film GoldenEye, where she played the sinister

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.420
Russian agent Xenia Onatopp.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.080
"Xenia Sergeyevna Onatopp."

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.479
"Onatopp?"

00:00:53.479 --> 00:00:54.559
"Onatopp."

00:00:54.559 --> 00:01:01.210
The character has become a fan favorite, consistently
ranking among the best Bond Girls ever.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.059
House on Haunted Hill

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:07.120
Following the success of GoldenEye, Janssen
was offered a number of roles.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.820
One of the most high profile was opposite
Geoffrey Rush as one half of the eccentric

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.730
couple running the show in the 1999 horror
remake House on Haunted Hill.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:21.760
The flick was a critical punching bag, but
has become a bit of a cult favorite anyway.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:22.760
X-Men

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.130
No matter what Janssen does in her career,
there are many fans who will always see her

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:30.960
as Jean Grey from 20th Century Fox's X-Men
franchise.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.830
Since 2000, Janssen has played the red-haired
mutant psychic multiple times, including the

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:43.090
original X-Men, X2: X-Men United in 2003,
and X-Men: The Last Stand in 2006, where she

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:43.760
was killed off.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:59.120
She later appeared in 2013's The Wolverine
as a figment of Logan's tortured imagination,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:04.310
but thanks to some time travel shenanigans,
she was returned to life for realsies in 2014's

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.690
X-Men: Days of Future Past.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.690
Nip/Tuck

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:13.970
A year after X2 hit theaters, Janssen landed
a recurring role in the second season of FX's

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.640
medical drama Nip/Tuck.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:21.380
The primary antagonist of that season, transgender
life coach Ava Moore became a key recurring

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.930
character, returning in season six for a major
arc.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.190
Hide and Seek

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:30.250
One of Janssen's stranger roles was in the
psychological thriller Hide and Seek, where

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.920
she played opposite Robert DeNiro.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.200
Her part as family friend Dr. Katherine Carson
wasn't large, but she figured prominently

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.660
in each of the film's five different endings.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.930
And you thought the X-Men movies were hard
to keep straight…

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:43.930
Taken

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.170
Twentieth Century Fox apparently didn't want
to let go of Janssen following the original

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:53.160
X-Men trilogy's conclusion, so they cast her
as Lenore "Lenny" Mills in their Taken series.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:59.120
In 2008, she played the wife of Liam Neeson's
Bryan Mills, whose daughter is taken captive.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.120
Bad move, fools.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.970
"I have a very particular set of skills.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.920
Skills I have acquired over a very long career.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.580
Skills that make me a nightmare for people
like you."

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.720
In 2012, she returned in a larger role, this
time as the victim of a revenge kidnapping.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.990
Neeson, of course, saves her.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:20.980
Too bad he couldn't get the job done in 2015's
Taken 3, where it's her life that gets taken

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.550
at the start of the film.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:27.040
One of these days, one of Janssen's characters
will actually survive a trilogy.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.260
Hansel &amp; Gretel: Witch Hunters

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:34.590
In-between Taken installments, Janssen starred
as the sinister grand witch Muriel in 2013's

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:38.890
Hansel &amp; Gretel: Witch Hunters, a re-imagining
of the classic fairy tale.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:43.490
The film wasn't exactly a critical favorite,
but it did well enough at the box office to

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:44.770
warrant a sequel.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:48.150
Whether or not Janssen will be involved hasn't
been announced yet.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:51.450
Even though her character died, don't count
her out.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.980
Hemlock Grove

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:58.730
In 2013, Janssen shifted away from movies
and back into television in a big way, starring

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:03.210
in a leading role in the groundbreaking Netflix
series Hemlock Grove, which was one of the

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:07.180
first digitally streamed shows to ever receive
an Emmy nomination.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:12.239
She played Olivia Godfrey, head of the sinister
Godfrey Institute for Biomedical Technologies,

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:15.580
for all three seasons before the show ended
in 2015.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.660
Yuck.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.820
How to Get Away with Murder

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:31.660
Before landing the lead in The Blacklist:
Redemption, Janssen took another juicy role

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:37.110
in the hit series How to Get Away with Murder,
playing attorney Eve Rothlow, a former friend

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:41.150
and lover of Viola Davis's lead character,
Annalise Keating.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:46.690
Still smarting from their breakup years ago,
Eve finally got over Annalise in season three,

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:47.710
and walked away.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:51.970
Whether or not she ever returns may depend
on how long The Blacklist: Redemption stays

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:52.970
on the air.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.020
Thanks for watching!

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.890
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.350
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

